{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaQStarClosedFormExclusion","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaQStarClosedFormExclusion","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.Monotone.Basic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaQStarClosedFormExclusion.qstarRootUniqueInAnchor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaQStarClosedFormExclusion.qstarRootUniqueInAnchor","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaQStarClosedFormExclusion.lean#L100-L109","doc":"Corollary: the landmark is *uniquely* determined by the anchor — two\nroots of the same measured anchor coincide. This is the non-trivial\ndirection (it uses the strict-monotone injectivity `StrictMonoOn.injOn`,\nso `q*` is a well-defined single-valued function of `Q_codata/m_e`, and by\n`qstarRootStrictMonoInAnchor` a genuinely varying one). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaQStarClosedFormExclusion.qstarRootStrictMonoInAnchor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaQStarClosedFormExclusion.qstarRootStrictMonoInAnchor","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaQStarClosedFormExclusion.lean#L83-L98","doc":"**Exclusion invariant (scope-(b)).** If the closed-form shape `Φ` is\nstrictly monotone on an interval `I` containing the roots, then the\nS-channel-zero landmark strictly tracks the experimental anchor:\na strictly larger measured anchor `Φ q₂` gives a strictly larger root\n`q₂`. Hence `q*` is a non-constant function of the measured input\n`R = Q_codata/m_e`, i.e. NOT an experiment-independent closed-form\nmathematical constant.\n\nThe `StrictMonoOn Φ I` hypothesis is the numerically-verified fact\n`Φ'(q*) ≠ 0` (sign-definite near `q*`, 50 dps); the implication is\nsorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaQStarClosedFormExclusion.qstarShape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaQStarClosedFormExclusion.qstarShape","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaQStarClosedFormExclusion.lean#L68-L81","doc":"The closed-form shape `Φ(q)` whose root `Φ(q) = Q_codata/m_e` is the\nS-channel-zero landmark `q*`. Elementary in `q` (rational · √ · cos) plus\nthe single external dilog constant `vol41 = Vol(4₁) = 2·Im Li₂(e^{iπ/3})`,\ncarried as a parameter. This `def` documents that the S-channel-zero\ncondition is a genuine *closed-form* transcendental equation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}